--- body ---
Repair `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py` after the upstream audit found
that pause sent stop, resume was declared absent, and MCP isError was lost
when structuredContent or a text body was extracted.

Pause and resume now forward the matching zotero_index actions. The adapter
returns the target reply instead of manufacturing checkpoint/durability claims.
MCP refusals retain their body and marker; ordinary verbs raise ToolError.
The embedding perturbation retains a refused build as evidence, allowing the
R22 work-counter checks to measure the expected hold without clearing it.

Regression coverage: tests/test_acceptance_adapter_zoteus.py. It exercises
both control actions and declarations, wrapped and bare MCP error replies,
structured and text bodies, refused query/status/control calls, expected
paused-build refusal, and a successful empty search.

Validation commands: python3 -m pytest tests/test_acceptance_adapter_zoteus.py
 tests/test_acceptance_adapter_zoteus_work_counters.py
 tests/test_acceptance_goal1_control.py tests/test_acceptance_durability.py -q;
 make check.

These are adapter and harness tests with synthetic MCP replies. No live Zotero
acceptance result or R22 grade is claimed. Historical results and UPSTREAM
remain their original observations.
